{
  "analysis": "Let's check the contents of `/sas/handoff/intake.pdf` or check if there are other files in `/sas` or `/disk`.
Let's see what is inside `/sas/handoff/intake.pdf` using `pdftotext` or `strings`.
Also let's explore `/disk` thoroughly.",
  "plan": "1. Run `pdftotext /sas/handoff/intake.pdf -` to view the intake form.\n2. Run `find /disk` or explore subdirectories in `/disk` to see what files exist on the host.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "pdftotext /sas/handoff/intake.pdf -\n",
      "duration": 0.2
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "find /disk -type f | head -n 100\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "There are exactly 13 files on `/disk`. Let's examine all of them in detail, along with any relevant tools or contents.

Let's list all files in `/disk` with `ls -la` recursively, and inspect every file content or run string analysis on binaries/logs.

The 13 files on `/disk` are:
1. `/disk/Users/Public/enc.exe` (Ransomware binary - T1486 / ALERT-03)
2. `/disk/Windows/Temp/lsass.dmp` (LSASS dump - T1003.001 / ALERT-02)
3. `/disk/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe` (Exploit implant - T1210 / ALERT-01 / CVE-2017-0144)
4. `/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/SECURITY.bak`
5. `/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/README.txt`
6. `/disk/Windows/System32/drivers/etc/hosts`
7. `/disk/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys` (SMBv1 driver baseline - T1210 / ALERT-04 / CHK-07)
8. `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA` (WMI event subscription persistence - T1546.003)
9. `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll` (DLL search-order hijack - T1574.001)
10. `/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/System.evtx` (Cleared event log / System.evtx - T1070.001)
11. `/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/Security-events.csv` (Security event log CSV)
12. `/disk/inetpub/logs/LogFiles/W3SVC1/u_ex.log` (IIS Web server log)
13. `/disk/ProgramData/Package Cache/inventory.csv`

Let's inspect text/CSV/log files first, then run `strings` on binary/data/log files.",
  "plan": "Inspect text files: `/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/README.txt`, `/disk/Windows/System32/drivers/etc/hosts`, `/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/Security-events.csv`, `/disk/inetpub/logs/LogFiles/W3SVC1/u_ex.log`, `/disk/ProgramData/Package Cache/inventory.csv`.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat /disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/README.txt\n",
      "duration": 0.2
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat /disk/Windows/System32/drivers/etc/hosts\n",
      "duration": 0.2
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat /disk/ProgramData/Package Cache/inventory.csv\n",
      "duration": 0.2
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat /disk/inetpub/logs/LogFiles/W3SVC1/u_ex.log\n",
      "duration": 0.2
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat /disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/Security-events.csv\n",
      "duration": 0.2
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "Notice how `cat /disk/ProgramData/Package Cache/inventory.csv` failed because of spaces in the filename (`Package Cache`).
Let's properly quote paths when running commands.
Let's inspect `/disk/ProgramData/Package Cache/inventory.csv`, and let's search `Security-events.csv`, `OBJECTS.DATA`, `wbemcomn.dll`, `System.evtx`, etc., using `strings` or specific search queries.",
  "plan": "1. Cat `/disk/ProgramData/Package Cache/inventory.csv`.\n2. Run `strings -e l` and `strings` on `/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/System.evtx` and `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA` and `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll`.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat \"/disk/ProgramData/Package Cache/inventory.csv\"\n",
      "duration": 0.2
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "strings \"/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA\" | grep -iE \"powershell|cmd|select|event|filter|consumer|script|exe|dll|http|198|203|cve\" | head -n 30\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "strings -e l \"/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA\" | grep -iE \"powershell|cmd|select|event|filter|consumer|script|exe|dll|http|198|203|cve\" | head -n 30\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "Let's check the remaining files in `/disk`:
- `/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/SECURITY.bak`
- `/disk/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys`

Let's inspect them with `cat` / `strings`.",
  "plan": "Cat or run strings on SECURITY.bak and srv.sys.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat \"/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/SECURITY.bak\"\n",
      "duration": 0.2
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat \"/disk/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys\"\n",
      "duration": 0.2
    }
  ]
}

